{"name":"Fluffy Duckling","hex":"#fcdf39","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fluffy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Covered with fluff.","Light; soft; airy."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone or something that has a fluffy texture.","A person who is superficial, who lacks depth or seriousness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fluffy"},{"term":"duckling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young duck.","A young female duck."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duckling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Duck","blocks":[{"text":"Duck is the common name for numerous species of waterfowl in the family Anatidae. Ducks are generally smaller and shorter-necked than swans and geese, which are members of the same family. Divided among several subfamilies, they are a form taxon; they do not represent a monophyletic group, since swans and geese are not considered ducks. Ducks are mostly aquatic birds, and may be found in both fresh water and sea water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Bucephala-albeola-010.jpg/330px-Bucephala-albeola-010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duck","wikidata":"Q3736439"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Pacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg/500px-Pacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Pacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg/1280px-Pacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Pacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg/500px-Pacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pacific black d